course: dictionary
lesson: 13978
title: Locally: nearby, in one spot, or made close by
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Locally means in or near the place where you are or live. «We buy our eggs locally, from the farm down the road.» The farm is close, so locally means nearby, not far away.
explain: Locally can also mean in one small part, not everywhere. «The nurse numbed my knee locally, so I felt nothing there.» Only the knee was numb, not the whole leg or the whole body. Ask yourself: is it one spot, or is it the whole thing?
explain: In shops and business, locally means made, grown or sold in the nearby area. «The café serves locally grown vegetables.» The vegetables did not travel far to get there. Look at the words around locally to see which meaning fits.
fact: Locally is an adverb, and it comes from the word local.
fact: «Locally» can mean nearby: «We shop locally.»
fact: «Locally» can mean in one small part: «The cream works locally, on the skin where you put it.»
fact: «Locally grown» means grown in the nearby area, not brought from far away.
fact: A local anaesthetic numbs one small part of the body, so it works locally.
exercise: «We buy our eggs locally, from the farm two miles away.» What does locally mean here? | *Nearby, in the area where we live | Only once a year | Very quickly | In a big city far away
exercise: «The bee sting hurt locally, just on my arm.» What does locally mean here? | Loudly | Far away from home | *In one small spot only | Everywhere in the body
exercise: «The shop sells locally made soap.» What does locally made mean? | Made of wood and very old | Made to be given away free | Made by robots in a factory overseas | *Made in the nearby area, not brought from far away
test: «Mum says, "Let's shop locally this week."» What does shop locally mean? | Only buy things online | Shop in another country | *Buy things from shops nearby | Never go shopping again
test: «The doctor numbed the cut locally, so Sam felt nothing in his finger.» What does locally mean here? | Very loudly | *Only in one small part, the finger | Across the whole country | At the top of a mountain
exam: «Sara's ankle is locally swollen after the fall.» What does locally mean here? | Made in the area | *In one small part, just the ankle | Nearby, in the town | Very quickly
